# Grain through Cursor Agent CLI

This is the project door for Cursor Agent CLI. Work from a terminal on the pier, commonly reached
from the Daylight DC-1 tablet through Termux, Mosh, and tmux. The GUI/editor lane is outside this
rule's scope.

Read [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) first. It names the shared project voice and points to the
canonical rules under [`.claude/rules/`](../../.claude/rules/). Do not fork those rules into a
second policy: read the specific canonical page when the task touches its subject.

The living Cursor CLI field guide is [`frontier/cursor-cli/README.md`](../../frontier/cursor-cli/README.md).
It owns the CLI/MOSH/Termux operating path and its boundary. The tracked project permission
surface is [`.cursor/cli.json`](../cli.json); personal model choice, login, and cached CLI state
stay outside Git in the user's Cursor config directory.

Keep changes small, inspect before editing, preserve unrelated work, and verify the result with a
named command or witness. Never place credentials, OAuth state, telemetry, or copied files from
`loops/cursor/` in the repository.
